5. Verify Databases for the role switch
SQL> connect sys/<SYS_PASSWORD>@PRIMCA as sysdba
Connected.
SQL> set line 200
select name, db_unique_name, database_role, open_mode, protection_mode, FORCE_LOGGING, SWITCHOVER_STATUS FROM gV$DATABASE;
SQL>
NAME      DB_UNIQUE_NAME                 DATABASE_ROLE    OPEN_MODE            PROTECTION_MODE      FORCE_LOGGING                           SWITCHOVER_STATUS
--------- ------------------------------ ---------------- -------------------- -------------------- --------------------------------------- --------------------
PRIMCA    PRIMCA                         PHYSICAL STANDBY READ ONLY WITH APPLY MAXIMUM PERFORMANCE  YES                                     NOT ALLOWED

SQL> connect sys/<SYS_PASSWORD>@STDBYCA as sysdba
Connected.
SQL> /

NAME      DB_UNIQUE_NAME                 DATABASE_ROLE    OPEN_MODE            PROTECTION_MODE      FORCE_LOGGING                           SWITCHOVER_STATUS
--------- ------------------------------ ---------------- -------------------- -------------------- --------------------------------------- --------------------
PRIMCA    STDBYCA                        PRIMARY          READ WRITE           MAXIMUM PERFORMANCE  YES                                     TO STANDBY


6. Failover

When to use: Primary is unavailable (crash, network failure, etc.).
Note: This may cause data loss depending on protection mode and lag.

Connect to Standby Database

[oracle@caoradb04 ~]$ dgmgrl
DGMGRL for Linux: Release 19.0.0.0.0 - Production on Thu Sep 17 16:04:15 2026
Version 19.32.0.0.0

Copyright (c) 1982, 2019, Oracle and/or its affiliates.  All rights reserved.

Welcome to DGMGRL, type "help" for information.
DGMGRL> connect sys/<SYS_PASSWORD>@PRIMCA
Connected to "PRIMCA"
Connected as SYSDBA.

DGMGRL> FAILOVER TO PRIMCA;
Performing failover NOW, please wait...
Failover succeeded, new primary is "primca"


